## Thursday night

::bg{location="roof" time="night"}
::music{playback="start" mood="romantic" volume="normal"}
::use{component="enter" who="sol" instance="use-001"}
@sol{code="0010" emotion="laughing"}: You came! I brought the good blanket. It's the same blanket. I washed it.
@narrator{code="0010"}: You lie side by side on the tar. The first one goes over before you're settled — a white scratch, there and gone.
::vfx{type="meteors"}
@sol{code="0020" emotion="fond"}: That's one. Say a number every time. Ines counts them for the log; I count them for me.

<branch id="count" prompt="The sky keeps striking matches.">
  <choice id="count" text="Count them with him, out loud">
    ::set{run.aff.sol += 2}
    @narrator{code="0020"}: Forty-one. Forty-two. Somewhere after sixty you both stop counting and just breathe out whenever one falls.
    @sol{code="0030" emotion="shy"}: This is the best one I've had. The shower, I mean. Obviously the shower.
  </choice>
  <choice id="quiet" text="Just watch">
    ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
    @narrator{code="0030"}: You watch until your eyes water. When you look over, he is watching you instead of the sky, and pretends he wasn't.
  </choice>
</branch>

@sol{code="0040"}: Same time next year? You'll be gone by then, I know. Just — same time.
